From f98239c0458dfe5eae45e2cb8f2ea8d4184075cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:35:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: Enable PDMA TX interrupts with a polling guard

Request the named PDMA IRQ for the EN7523 TSO v2 datapath. Mask and
acknowledge observed TX_DONE events in the hard IRQ, then recycle through
TX NAPI. Rearm after NAPI completion and check for latched events so work
arriving while masked cannot be lost. Serialize scheduling, rearming and
shutdown with an IRQ-safe lock, and synchronize IRQs before stopping NAPI
or resetting the dedicated TDMA engine. Free the IRQ on cleanup even when
reset fails and DMA buffers must be retained.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 .../device_drivers/ethernet/airoha/tso.rst         |  63 +++++-
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c           |   5 +-
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_tso.c           | 238 +++++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_tso.h           |  16 ++
 4 files changed, 303 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/networking/device_drivers/ethernet/airoha/tso.rst b/Documentation/networking/device_drivers/ethernet/airoha/tso.rst
--- a/Documentation/networking/device_drivers/ethernet/airoha/tso.rst
+++ b/Documentation/networking/device_drivers/ethernet/airoha/tso.rst
@@ -36,9 +36,10 @@ using QDMA. Setting only the TSO bit on a fragmented QDMA chain does not
 implement v2. When the option is disabled, EN7523 GDM2 retains software
 segmentation and linear TX.
 
-PDMA completion uses timer-driven TX NAPI, following the polling mode
-selected by the 32-bit SDK. It does not require a new interrupt assignment
-or a device-tree node. Both DONE and the DMA index must indicate completion
+PDMA completion normally uses timer-driven TX NAPI, following the polling
+mode selected by the 32-bit SDK. The EN7523 IRQ path described below
+uses the existing named ``pdma`` interrupt. Both DONE and the DMA index must
+indicate completion
 before a buffer is unmapped. Polling continues while descriptors remain,
 including after the final packet of a connection. Interface shutdown and
 PON channel retirement drain PDMA and reset it before releasing buffers
@@ -76,3 +77,59 @@ To return an enabled build to linear software TX during diagnosis, disable
 SG and TSO together, for example::
 
   ethtool -K pon0 tso off gso off sg off
+
+EN7523 PDMA TX interrupts
+------------------------
+
+PDMA TX interrupts are enabled by default on EN7523 with TSO v2 enabled.
+The driver requests the Ethernet interrupt named ``pdma`` (SPI 64
+in the EN7523 DTS) and enables TX0_DONE/TX1_DONE at FE + 0xa28. Other SoCs
+keep the existing polling path. Missing IRQ names or request failures also
+fall back to polling. A deferred IRQ provider defers probe.
+
+The hard IRQ acknowledges observed TX_DONE bits using W1C, masks both TX
+interrupt sources, and schedules TX NAPI. NAPI recycles buffers and rearms
+the IRQ after completing its work, checking for events latched while the
+interrupt was masked. A 1 ms timer remains armed while buffers are pending,
+so missing IRQ delivery or delayed descriptor writeback cannot strand the
+last transmission. The polling-only path retains its 100 us interval.
+Shutdown masks and synchronizes the IRQ before disabling NAPI or resetting
+the dedicated TDMA engine. Restart reenables the IRQ after NAPI is ready.
+
+After boot, check registration and record counters before and after traffic::
+
+  dmesg | grep 'PDMA TX IRQ'
+  grep airoha-pdma /proc/interrupts
+  ethtool -S eth0 | grep pdma_
+
+Run sustained and short TCP tests in both directions, then check that PDMA
+CPU/DMA indices converge and BQL inflight bytes return to zero. Repeat
+interface stop/start and optical channel retirement while traffic is active.
+
+The ethtool counters are shared by all GDM interfaces:
+
+* ``pdma_irq_mode`` is 1 when the IRQ was successfully requested. It does
+  not establish IRQ delivery; ``pdma_irq_events`` counts handled IRQs.
+* ``pdma_irq_tx0`` and ``pdma_irq_tx1`` count observed TX_DONE bits in the
+  hard IRQ handler. Coalesced events are not individual packet counts.
+* ``pdma_timer_fires`` counts timer callbacks which found pending buffers.
+* ``pdma_irq_reclaimed`` counts descriptors reclaimed by NAPI scheduled by
+  the hard IRQ. ``pdma_poll_reclaimed`` counts descriptors reclaimed by
+  polling or the software status recheck after rearming. Attribution follows
+  the NAPI scheduling source until completion; it is not per-packet timing.
+  Synchronous shutdown draining is excluded from both counters.
+* ``pdma_tx_packets`` counts skbs submitted to PDMA, including ordinary SG.
+  ``pdma_gso_packets`` counts the subset submitted with GSO metadata.
+
+IRQ delivery is established when ``pdma_irq_events`` and the corresponding
+``/proc/interrupts`` count increase. Positive ``pdma_irq_reclaimed`` confirms
+that IRQ-scheduled NAPI recycled descriptors. If these stay zero while
+``pdma_poll_reclaimed`` grows, the guard is doing the recycling; successful
+traffic alone does not validate the IRQ. Some polling reclamation can still
+occur with a working IRQ due to delayed writeback or the status recheck.
+
+The read-only module parameter ``pdma_irq=0`` restores polling-only
+operation at the next driver load. For an OpenWrt module, append that option
+to the airoha-eth entry in the module loader configuration and reboot. For
+a built-in driver, use ``airoha_eth.pdma_irq=0`` on the kernel command
+line. The parameter cannot be switched while the driver is running.
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -8609,7 +8609,8 @@ static int airoha_get_sset_count(struct net_device *netdev, int sset)
 	if (sset != ETH_SS_STATS)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
-	return hweight32(dev->eth->fe_irq_mask);
+	return hweight32(dev->eth->fe_irq_mask) +
+	       airoha_tso_get_sset_count(dev->eth);
 }
 
 static void airoha_get_strings(struct net_device *netdev, u32 sset, u8 *data)
@@ -8623,6 +8624,7 @@ static void airoha_get_strings(struct net_device *netdev, u32 sset, u8 *data)
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(airoha_fe_irq_names); i++)
 		if (dev->eth->fe_irq_mask & BIT(i))
 			ethtool_puts(&data, airoha_fe_irq_names[i]);
+	airoha_tso_get_strings(dev->eth, data);
 }
 
 static void airoha_get_ethtool_stats(struct net_device *netdev,
@@ -8634,6 +8636,7 @@ static void airoha_get_ethtool_stats(struct net_device *netdev,
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(airoha_fe_irq_names); i++)
 		if (dev->eth->fe_irq_mask & BIT(i))
 			*data++ = atomic64_read(&dev->eth->fe_irq_stats[i]);
+	airoha_tso_get_stats(dev->eth, data);
 }
 
 static void airoha_ethtool_get_mac_stats(struct net_device *netdev,
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_tso.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_tso.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_tso.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_tso.c
@@ -1,9 +1,12 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 /* EcoNet QDMA TSO v1 and EN7523 PDMA TSO v2. */
 #include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/ethtool.h>
 #include <linux/hrtimer.h>
+#include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/ip.h>
 #include <linux/ipv6.h>
+#include <linux/moduleparam.h>
 #include <linux/reset.h>
 #include <linux/tcp.h>
 #include <net/ip.h>
@@ -23,7 +26,34 @@
 #define TSO_DELAY_INT		0xa0c
 #define TSO_INT_STATUS		0xa20
 #define TSO_INT_MASK		0xa28
+#define TSO_TX_DONE		GENMASK(1, 0)
 #define TSO_POLL_NS		(100 * NSEC_PER_USEC)
+#define TSO_IRQ_GUARD_NS		NSEC_PER_MSEC
+
+enum airoha_tso_stat {
+	TSO_STAT_IRQ_MODE,
+	TSO_STAT_IRQ_EVENTS,
+	TSO_STAT_IRQ_TX0,
+	TSO_STAT_IRQ_TX1,
+	TSO_STAT_TIMER_FIRES,
+	TSO_STAT_IRQ_RECLAIMED,
+	TSO_STAT_POLL_RECLAIMED,
+	TSO_STAT_TX_PACKETS,
+	TSO_STAT_GSO_PACKETS,
+	TSO_STAT_COUNT,
+};
+
+static const char airoha_tso_stat_names[TSO_STAT_COUNT][ETH_GSTRING_LEN] = {
+	"pdma_irq_mode",
+	"pdma_irq_events",
+	"pdma_irq_tx0",
+	"pdma_irq_tx1",
+	"pdma_timer_fires",
+	"pdma_irq_reclaimed",
+	"pdma_poll_reclaimed",
+	"pdma_tx_packets",
+	"pdma_gso_packets",
+};
 
 struct airoha_tso_entry {
 	dma_addr_t dma;
@@ -49,12 +79,38 @@ struct airoha_tso {
 	struct hrtimer timer;
 	/* Serialize flush and reset of the shared PDMA engine. */
 	struct mutex mutex;
+	/* Serialize IRQ masking, NAPI scheduling and stop/restart. */
+	spinlock_t irq_lock;
+	atomic64_t stats[TSO_STAT_COUNT];
+	int irq;
+	bool poll_from_irq;
 	bool running;
 	bool napi_enabled;
 	bool programmed;
 	u8 next_ring;
 };
 
+int airoha_tso_get_sset_count(struct airoha_eth *eth)
+{
+	return eth->tso ? TSO_STAT_COUNT : 0;
+}
+
+void airoha_tso_get_strings(struct airoha_eth *eth, u8 *data)
+{
+	if (eth->tso)
+		memcpy(data, airoha_tso_stat_names, sizeof(airoha_tso_stat_names));
+}
+
+void airoha_tso_get_stats(struct airoha_eth *eth, u64 *data)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	if (!eth->tso)
+		return;
+	for (i = 0; i < TSO_STAT_COUNT; i++)
+		data[i] = atomic64_read(&eth->tso->stats[i]);
+}
+
 enum airoha_tso_version airoha_tso_version(struct airoha_eth *eth)
 {
 	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_TSO))
@@ -223,18 +279,90 @@ static void airoha_tso_wake(struct airoha_tso *tso,
 	}
 }
 
+static void airoha_tso_mask_irq(struct airoha_tso *tso)
+{
+	airoha_fe_wr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_MASK, 0);
+	airoha_fe_rr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_MASK);
+}
+
+static void airoha_tso_ack_irq(struct airoha_tso *tso, u32 status)
+{
+	airoha_fe_wr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_STATUS, status);
+	airoha_fe_rr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_STATUS);
+}
+
+/* Called with irq_lock held and local IRQs disabled. */
+static void airoha_tso_schedule(struct airoha_tso *tso, bool from_irq)
+{
+	if (!tso->running)
+		return;
+	if (tso->irq)
+		airoha_tso_mask_irq(tso);
+	if (napi_schedule_prep(&tso->napi)) {
+		tso->poll_from_irq = from_irq;
+		__napi_schedule(&tso->napi);
+	}
+}
+
+static void airoha_tso_arm_timer(struct airoha_tso *tso)
+{
+	if (!hrtimer_active(&tso->timer))
+		hrtimer_start(&tso->timer,
+			      ns_to_ktime(tso->irq ? TSO_IRQ_GUARD_NS : TSO_POLL_NS),
+			      HRTIMER_MODE_REL);
+}
+
+static irqreturn_t airoha_tso_irq(int irq, void *data)
+{
+	struct airoha_tso *tso = data;
+	unsigned long flags;
+	u32 status;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
+	status = airoha_fe_rr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_STATUS) & TSO_TX_DONE;
+	status &= airoha_fe_rr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_MASK);
+	if (!status) {
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
+		return IRQ_NONE;
+	}
+	airoha_tso_mask_irq(tso);
+	airoha_tso_ack_irq(tso, status);
+	atomic64_inc(&tso->stats[TSO_STAT_IRQ_EVENTS]);
+	if (status & BIT(0))
+		atomic64_inc(&tso->stats[TSO_STAT_IRQ_TX0]);
+	if (status & BIT(1))
+		atomic64_inc(&tso->stats[TSO_STAT_IRQ_TX1]);
+	airoha_tso_schedule(tso, true);
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
+	return IRQ_HANDLED;
+}
+
 static enum hrtimer_restart airoha_tso_timer(struct hrtimer *timer)
 {
 	struct airoha_tso *tso = container_of(timer, struct airoha_tso, timer);
+	unsigned long flags;
 
-	if (READ_ONCE(tso->running))
-		napi_schedule(&tso->napi);
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
+	if (tso->running && airoha_tso_pending(tso)) {
+		atomic64_inc(&tso->stats[TSO_STAT_TIMER_FIRES]);
+		if (tso->irq) {
+			u32 status;
+
+			airoha_tso_mask_irq(tso);
+			status = airoha_fe_rr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_STATUS) & TSO_TX_DONE;
+			airoha_tso_ack_irq(tso, status);
+		}
+		airoha_tso_schedule(tso, false);
+	}
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
 	return HRTIMER_NORESTART;
 }
 
 static int airoha_tso_poll(struct napi_struct *napi, int budget)
 {
 	struct airoha_tso *tso = container_of(napi, struct airoha_tso, napi);
+	bool from_irq = tso->poll_from_irq;
+	unsigned long flags;
 	int done = 0, i;
 
 	if (!budget)
@@ -243,11 +371,30 @@ static int airoha_tso_poll(struct napi_struct *napi, int budget)
 		done += airoha_tso_reap(tso, (tso->next_ring + i) % TSO_RINGS,
 				       budget - done);
 	tso->next_ring ^= 1;
-	if (done)
+	if (done) {
+		atomic64_add(done, &tso->stats[from_irq ? TSO_STAT_IRQ_RECLAIMED :
+						       TSO_STAT_POLL_RECLAIMED]);
 		airoha_tso_wake(tso, NULL);
-	if (done < budget && napi_complete_done(napi, 0) &&
-	    READ_ONCE(tso->running) && airoha_tso_pending(tso))
-		hrtimer_start(&tso->timer, ns_to_ktime(TSO_POLL_NS), HRTIMER_MODE_REL);
+	}
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
+	if (done < budget && napi_complete_done(napi, done) && tso->running) {
+		if (tso->irq) {
+			u32 status;
+
+			airoha_fe_wr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_MASK, TSO_TX_DONE);
+			airoha_fe_rr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_MASK);
+			/* Catch events latched while NAPI owned the masked rings. */
+			status = airoha_fe_rr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_STATUS) & TSO_TX_DONE;
+			if (status) {
+				airoha_tso_mask_irq(tso);
+				airoha_tso_ack_irq(tso, status);
+				airoha_tso_schedule(tso, false);
+			}
+		}
+		if (airoha_tso_pending(tso))
+			airoha_tso_arm_timer(tso);
+	}
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
 	return done;
 }
 
@@ -259,6 +406,7 @@ netdev_tx_t airoha_tso_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *dev,
 	struct netdev_queue *txq = skb_get_tx_queue(dev, skb);
 	struct airoha_tso_ring *q;
 	unsigned int n = 1 + skb_shinfo(skb)->nr_frags, i;
+	unsigned long flags;
 	u16 index;
 
 	if (unlikely(!tso || ring >= TSO_RINGS || !skb_headlen(skb) ||
@@ -310,6 +458,9 @@ netdev_tx_t airoha_tso_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *dev,
 	dev_hold(dev);
 	q->head = index;
 	q->queued += n;
+	atomic64_inc(&tso->stats[TSO_STAT_TX_PACKETS]);
+	if (skb_is_gso(skb))
+		atomic64_inc(&tso->stats[TSO_STAT_GSO_PACKETS]);
 	skb_tx_timestamp(skb);
 	netdev_tx_sent_queue(txq, skb->len);
 	if (TSO_DESCS - q->queued <= MAX_SKB_FRAGS + 1)
@@ -317,7 +468,14 @@ netdev_tx_t airoha_tso_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *dev,
 	dma_wmb();
 	airoha_fe_wr(tso->eth, TSO_RING_CPU(ring), q->head);
 	spin_unlock_bh(&q->lock);
-	napi_schedule(&tso->napi);
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
+	if (tso->running) {
+		if (tso->irq)
+			airoha_tso_arm_timer(tso);
+		else
+			airoha_tso_schedule(tso, false);
+	}
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
 	return NETDEV_TX_OK;
 
 unmap:
@@ -361,15 +519,59 @@ static void airoha_tso_program(struct airoha_tso *tso)
 	tso->programmed = true;
 }
 
+static int airoha_tso_request_irq(struct airoha_tso *tso)
+{
+	struct device *dev = tso->eth->dev;
+	int irq, err;
+
+	irq = platform_get_irq_byname_optional(to_platform_device(dev), "pdma");
+	if (irq == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+		return irq;
+	if (irq < 0) {
+		dev_warn(dev, "PDMA IRQ unavailable (%d); using TX polling\n", irq);
+		return 0;
+	}
+	err = request_irq(irq, airoha_tso_irq, 0, "airoha-pdma", tso);
+	if (err) {
+		dev_warn(dev, "PDMA IRQ request failed (%d); using TX polling\n", err);
+		return 0;
+	}
+	tso->irq = irq;
+	atomic64_set(&tso->stats[TSO_STAT_IRQ_MODE], 1);
+	dev_info(dev, "PDMA TX IRQ enabled, IRQ %d, 1 ms polling guard\n", irq);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static void airoha_tso_start(struct airoha_tso *tso)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+
+	napi_enable(&tso->napi);
+	tso->napi_enabled = true;
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
+	WRITE_ONCE(tso->running, true);
+	if (tso->irq) {
+		airoha_fe_wr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_MASK, TSO_TX_DONE);
+		airoha_fe_rr(tso->eth, TSO_INT_MASK);
+	}
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
+}
+
 /* Stop producers before draining, including during ndo_stop/BQL reset and
  * GPON retirement. A timed-out engine is reset before any map is released.
  */
 static int airoha_tso_quiesce(struct airoha_tso *tso)
 {
 	unsigned long timeout = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(100);
+	unsigned long flags;
 	int i, err;
 
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
 	WRITE_ONCE(tso->running, false);
+	airoha_tso_mask_irq(tso);
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tso->irq_lock, flags);
+	if (tso->irq)
+		synchronize_irq(tso->irq);
 	for (i = 0; i < TSO_RINGS; i++) {
 		spin_lock_bh(&tso->ring[i].lock);
 		spin_unlock_bh(&tso->ring[i].lock);
@@ -428,9 +630,7 @@ void airoha_tso_flush(struct airoha_eth *eth, struct net_device *stopping)
 		goto out;
 	}
 	airoha_tso_program(tso);
-	napi_enable(&tso->napi);
-	tso->napi_enabled = true;
-	WRITE_ONCE(tso->running, true);
+	airoha_tso_start(tso);
 	airoha_tso_wake(tso, stopping);
 out:
 	mutex_unlock(&tso->mutex);
@@ -439,11 +639,15 @@ void airoha_tso_flush(struct airoha_eth *eth, struct net_device *stopping)
 void airoha_tso_cleanup(struct airoha_eth *eth)
 {
 	struct airoha_tso *tso = eth->tso;
-	int i;
+	int i, err = 0;
 
 	if (!tso)
 		return;
-	if (tso->programmed && airoha_tso_quiesce(tso)) {
+	if (tso->programmed)
+		err = airoha_tso_quiesce(tso);
+	if (tso->irq)
+		free_irq(tso->irq, tso);
+	if (err) {
 		/* Retain DMA buffers rather than free memory still owned by a
 		 * controller which could not be stopped/reset.
 		 */
@@ -484,6 +688,9 @@ int airoha_tso_init(struct airoha_eth *eth)
 	tso->rst = rst;
 	eth->tso = tso;
 	mutex_init(&tso->mutex);
+	spin_lock_init(&tso->irq_lock);
+	for (i = 0; i < TSO_STAT_COUNT; i++)
+		atomic64_set(&tso->stats[i], 0);
 	hrtimer_setup(&tso->timer, airoha_tso_timer, CLOCK_MONOTONIC,
 		      HRTIMER_MODE_REL);
 	netif_napi_add_tx(eth->napi_dev, &tso->napi, airoha_tso_poll);
@@ -506,9 +713,10 @@ int airoha_tso_init(struct airoha_eth *eth)
 	if (err)
 		goto error;
 	airoha_tso_program(tso);
-	napi_enable(&tso->napi);
-	tso->napi_enabled = true;
-	WRITE_ONCE(tso->running, true);
+	err = airoha_tso_request_irq(tso);
+	if (err)
+		goto error;
+	airoha_tso_start(tso);
 	return 0;
 error:
 	airoha_tso_cleanup(eth);
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_tso.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_tso.h
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_tso.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_tso.h
@@ -9,6 +9,9 @@
 /* Build airoha_tso.o only when CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_TSO is enabled. */
 #ifdef CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_TSO
 enum airoha_tso_version airoha_tso_version(struct airoha_eth *eth);
+int airoha_tso_get_sset_count(struct airoha_eth *eth);
+void airoha_tso_get_strings(struct airoha_eth *eth, u8 *data);
+void airoha_tso_get_stats(struct airoha_eth *eth, u64 *data);
 netdev_features_t airoha_tso_features_check(struct sk_buff *skb,
 					    struct net_device *dev,
 					    netdev_features_t features);
@@ -20,6 +23,19 @@ void airoha_tso_flush(struct airoha_eth *eth, struct net_device *stopping);
 netdev_tx_t airoha_tso_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *dev,
 			    unsigned int ring, u32 msg0, u32 msg1);
 #else
+static inline int airoha_tso_get_sset_count(struct airoha_eth *eth)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static inline void airoha_tso_get_strings(struct airoha_eth *eth, u8 *data)
+{
